{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And they brought the Mishkan to Moses, the Tent and all its vessels</b> — the syntactic structure of the verse is as though there were a vav: \"And they brought the Mishkan to Moses, and the Tent and all its vessels.\" For the curtains of twisted linen (שֵׁשׁ מָשְׁזָר) are themselves the Mishkan, as it says (Exodus 26:1), \"And you shall make the Mishkan of ten curtains of twisted linen,\" and it says of them (Exodus 26:6), \"And you shall join the curtains together, and the Mishkan shall be one.\" And the curtains of goat hair are the Tent, as it says of them, \"And you shall make curtains of goats' hair for a Tent upon the Mishkan\" (Exodus 26:7), \"And you shall join the Tent, and it shall be one\" (Exodus 26:11). And likewise, \"the Mishkan, its Tent and its covering\" (Exodus 35:11) — \"and its Tent.\" So too here: \"And they brought the Mishkan to Moses, and the Tent and all its vessels,\" for he mentions the names of everything. And sometimes the entire House is called the Tent of Meeting, as it says (Exodus 31:6–7), \"And they shall make all that I have commanded you — the Tent of Meeting and the Ark of the Testimony,\" for the Tent of Meeting is the House in its entirety, where He would meet with him there. And likewise, \"all the vessels of the service of the Mishkan for the Tent of Meeting\" (Exodus 39:40)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:22:23.265356876Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}